</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="S6.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Quartile performance analysis on post-training claims also displays the Dunning-Kruger effect pattern, serving as a robustness check.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/error-bars-plot.png" id="S6.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/616;" width="476" height="616" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="S6.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The full set of results investigating the error distributions of the models across all prompts.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F17" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/balanced-acc.png" id="S6.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/495;" width="476" height="495" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F17.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 17</span>: </span><span id="S6.F17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The balanced accuracy score for models as a robustness check to account for imbalanced true and false statements in the original dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F18" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/hybrid_language_comparison_selective_accuracy.png" id="S6.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F18.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 18</span>: </span><span id="S6.F18.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Statistical significance of pairwise comparisons for selective accuracy across all model-language combinations.
Each cell represents a Holm-Bonferroni adjusted <math id="S6.F18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value from the appropriate statistical test: McNemar’s test for within-language comparisons (e.g., GPT-4-en vs. Llama-7B-en) and the Chi-Squared test for cross-language comparisons (e.g., GPT-4-en vs. GPT-4-es). The selective accuracy metric includes only claims where both models provided a definitive (‘True’ or ‘False’) response. Chi-Squared tests were only performed when all expected cell frequencies were <math id="S6.F18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>.
Color key: dark wine (<math id="S6.F18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), and light grey (<math id="S6.F18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F19" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/hybrid_language_comparison_abstention-free_accuracy.png" id="S6.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F19.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 19</span>: </span><span id="S6.F19.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Statistical significance of pairwise comparisons for abstention-free accuracy across all model-language combinations.
For this metric, a response was considered successful (1) if the model’s judgment was correct or if it abstained. The appropriate statistical test was selected for each pair: McNemar’s test for within-language comparisons and the Chi-Squared test for cross-language comparisons. All <math id="S6.F19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values were collectively adjusted using the Holm-Bonferroni method.
Color key: dark wine (<math id="S6.F19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), and light grey (<math id="S6.F19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F20" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/hybrid_language_comparison_certainty_rate.png" id="S6.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 20</span>: </span><span id="S6.F20.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Statistical significance of pairwise comparisons for the Certainty Rate across all model-language combinations.
The Certainty Rate measures a model’s propensity to provide a definitive answer (not ‘Other’). Each cell shows the Holm-Bonferroni adjusted <math id="S6.F20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value derived from either a McNemar’s test (for within-language pairs) or a Chi-Squared test (for cross-language pairs), with the latter only performed when expected frequencies were sufficient.
Color key: dark wine (<math id="S6.F20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), and light grey (<math id="S6.F20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F21" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/models_on_prompt-4_selective_accuracy.png" id="S6.F21.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/401;" width="476" height="401" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 21</span>: </span><span id="S6.F21.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">P-values distribution for selective accuracy evaluated using McNemar’s test across pairs of Models with adjustments for multiple comparisons using Holm-Bonferroni method (including <span id="S6.F21.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">o1-preview</span>) for Prompt 4. Color keys: dark wine (<math id="S6.F21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq 0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq 0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), light grey (<math id="S6.F21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F22" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/models_on_prompt-4_abstention-free_accuracy.png" id="S6.F22.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/401;" width="476" height="401" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F22.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 22</span>: </span><span id="S6.F22.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">P-values distribution for abstention-friendly accuracy evaluated using McNemar’s test across pairs of Models with adjustments for multiple comparisons using the Holm-Bonferroni method (including <span id="S6.F22.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">o1-preview</span>) for Prompt 4. Color keys: dark wine (<math id="S6.F22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq 0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq 0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), light grey (<math id="S6.F22.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F23" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/models_on_prompt-4_certainty_rate.png" id="S6.F23.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/401;" width="476" height="401" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F23.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 23</span>: </span><span id="S6.F23.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">P-values distribution for certainty rate evaluated using McNemar’s test across pairs of Models with adjustments for multiple comparisons using Holm-Bonferroni method (including <span id="S6.F23.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">o1-preview</span>) for Prompt 4. Color keys: dark wine (<math id="S6.F23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq 0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq 0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F23.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F23.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), light grey (<math id="S6.F23.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F24" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/cross_language_comparison_selective_accuracy.png" id="S6.F24.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/380;" width="476" height="380" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F24.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 24</span>: </span><span id="S6.F24.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Statistical significance of pairwise comparisons for selective accuracy between languages, aggregating data across all models on prompts 1, 2, and 3.
Each cell represents the Holm-Bonferroni adjusted <math id="S6.F24.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value from a Chi-Squared test comparing the performance of two languages. Selective accuracy includes only claims where a definitive (‘True’ or ‘False’) response was given. The total sample sizes for this metric after filtering were: English (<math id="S6.F24.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=28,319" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>28,319</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=28,319</annotation></semantics></math>), Spanish (<math id="S6.F24.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=5,800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5,800</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=5,800</annotation></semantics></math>), Hindi (<math id="S6.F24.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2,911" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2,911</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2,911</annotation></semantics></math>), and Portuguese (<math id="S6.F24.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=10,151" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10,151</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=10,151</annotation></semantics></math>).
Color key: dark wine (<math id="S6.F24.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F24.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F24.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), and light grey (<math id="S6.F24.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F25" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/cross_language_comparison_abstention-free_accuracy.png" id="S6.F25.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/380;" width="476" height="380" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F25.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 25</span>: </span><span id="S6.F25.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Statistical significance of pairwise comparisons for abstention-friendly accuracy between languages, aggregating data across all models on prompts 1, 2, and 3.
For this metric, a response was considered successful if it was correct or an abstention (‘other’). Each cell displays the Holm-Bonferroni adjusted <math id="S6.F25.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value from a pairwise Chi-Squared test. The total sample sizes were: English (<math id="S6.F25.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=42,456" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>42,456</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=42,456</annotation></semantics></math>), Spanish (<math id="S6.F25.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=12,600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12,600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=12,600</annotation></semantics></math>), Hindi (<math id="S6.F25.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=9,576" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9,576</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=9,576</annotation></semantics></math>), and Portuguese (<math id="S6.F25.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=17,616" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17,616</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=17,616</annotation></semantics></math>).
Color key: dark wine (<math id="S6.F25.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F25.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F25.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), and light grey (<math id="S6.F25.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F26" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08803v1/figures/cross_language_comparison_certainty_rate.png" id="S6.F26.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/380;" width="476" height="380" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F26.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 26</span>: </span><span id="S6.F26.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Statistical significance of pairwise comparisons for the Certainty Rate between languages, aggregating data across all models on prompts 1, 2, and 3.
The Certainty Rate measures the proportion of non-abstaining (i.e., not ‘Other’) responses. Each cell shows the Holm-Bonferroni adjusted <math id="S6.F26.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value from a pairwise Chi-Squared test. The total sample sizes were: English (<math id="S6.F26.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=42,456" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>42,456</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=42,456</annotation></semantics></math>), Spanish (<math id="S6.F26.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=12,600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12,600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=12,600</annotation></semantics></math>), Hindi (<math id="S6.F26.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=9,576" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9,576</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=9,576</annotation></semantics></math>), and Portuguese (<math id="S6.F26.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=17,616" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17,616</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=17,616</annotation></semantics></math>).
Color key: dark wine (<math id="S6.F26.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>), light yellow (<math id="S6.F26.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01\leq p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01\leq p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), light blue (<math id="S6.F26.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\leq p&lt;0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\leq p&lt;0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), and light grey (<math id="S6.F26.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.10</annotation></semantics></math>).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
